the cost of the original Geralf's activated ability.","oracle_id":"0a0743b0-07c2-4e11-8b30-6b1b8156bdd0","published_at":"2021-11-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Dina's first ability triggers only once for each life gain event, no matter how much life was gained.","oracle_id":"2121bcb4-f5fe-447f-9112-c7e5b5c45baf","published_at":"2021-04-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Each creature with lifelink dealing combat damage causes a separate life gain event. For example, if two creatures you control with lifelink deal combat damage at the same time, a \"whenever you gain life\" ability will trigger twice. However, if a single creature you control with lifelink deals combat damage to multiple creatures, players, and/or planeswalkers at the same time (perhaps because it has trample or was blocked by more than one creature), the ability will trigger only once.","oracle_id":"2121bcb4-f5fe-447f-9112-c7e5b5c45baf","published_at":"2021-04-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"When Dina's first ability resolves, each opponent loses only 1 life, no matter how much life was gained.","oracle_id":"2121bcb4-f5fe-447f-9112-c7e5b5c45baf","published_at":"2021-04-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"X is the power the creature had when it was on the battlefield, not the power it has in the graveyard.","oracle_id":"2121bcb4-f5fe-447f-9112-c7e5b5c45baf","published_at":"2021-04-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Use the toughness of the sacrificed creature as it last existed on the battlefield to determine how many +1/+1 counters to put on Scourge of Skola Vale.","oracle_id":"725d7374-4ea8-4aef-ac09-8dcb5d8dcad1","published_at":"2014-02-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an attacking creature loses haste, perhaps because Fervor leaves the battlefield after attackers have been declared, it won't be removed from combat.","oracle_id":"8e0cea9c-3110-4728-9378-76849e33bb90","published_at":"2012-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"\"Flashback [cost]\" means \"You may cast this card from your graveyard by paying [cost] rather than paying its mana cost\" and \"If the flashback cost was paid, exile this card instead of putting it anywhere else any time it would leave the stack.\"","oracle_id":"9e2adca5-f39c-4a09-bcce-8238ebac2c4a","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A spell cast using flashback will always be exiled afterward, whether it resolves, is countered, or leaves the stack in some other way.","oracle_id":"9e2adca5-f39c-4a09-bcce-8238ebac2c4a","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a card with flashback is put into your graveyard during your turn, you can cast it if it's legal to do so before any other player can take any actions.","oracle_id":"9e2adca5-f39c-4a09-bcce-8238ebac2c4a","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"To determine the total cost of a spell, start with the mana cost or alternative cost (such as a flashback cost) you're paying, add any cost increases, then apply any cost reductions. The mana value of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.","oracle_id":"9e2adca5-f39c-4a09-bcce-8238ebac2c4a","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can cast a spell using flashback even if it was somehow put into your graveyard without having been cast.","oracle_id":"9e2adca5-f39c-4a09-bcce-8238ebac2c4a","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You must still follow any timing restrictions and permissions, including those based on the card's type. For instance, you can cast a sorcery using flashback only when you could normally cast a sorcery.","oracle_id":"9e2adca5-f39c-4a09-bcce-8238ebac2c4a","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Any “enters” triggered ability of the copied creature will trigger when the token enters the battlefield. Any “as [this creature] enters” or “[this creature] enters with” abilities of the chosen creature will also work.","oracle_id":"9e2adca5-f39c-4a09-bcce-8238ebac2c4a","published_at":"2025-01-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the copied creature has {X} in its mana cost, X is considered to be 0.","oracle_id":"9e2adca5-f39c-4a09-bcce-8238ebac2c4a","published_at":"2025-01-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the copied creature is a token, the token that’s created copies the original characteristics of that token as stated by the effect that created the token.","oracle_id":"9e2adca5-f39c-4a09-bcce-8238ebac2c4a","published_at":"2025-01-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the copied creature is copying something else, then the token enters the battlefield as whatever that creature copied.","oracle_id":"9e2adca5-f39c-4a09-bcce-8238ebac2c4a","published_at":"2025-01-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The token copies exactly what was printed on the original creature and nothing else (unless that creature is copying something else or is a token; see below). It doesn’t copy whether that creature is tapped or untapped, whether it has any counters on it or Auras and Equipment attached to it, or any non-copy effects that have changed its power, toughness, types, color, or so on.","oracle_id":"9e2adca5-f39c-4a09-bcce-8238ebac2c4a","published_at":"2025-01-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Use the sacrificed creature’s toughness when it was last on the battlefield to determine the value of X.","oracle_id":"b209b4ae-ceba-4a98-b307-222d3c78f8a1","published_at":"2012-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"An activated ability has a \"Cost: Effect\" format. Look for the colon. A triggered ability starts with \"when\", \"whenever\", or \"at\".","oracle_id":"b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"It can target delayed triggered abilities. For example, a card that says \"Whenever a player cycles a card, you may exile target creature. If you do, return that creature to the battlefield at the beginning of the end step.\" triggers when a player cycles a card and creates a delayed trigger that happens at the beginning of the end step. You can choose to target the \"at the beginning of the end step\" trigger when it is placed on the stack at end of turn.","oracle_id":"b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Turn-based actions and special actions like the normal card draw, combat damage, or turning a face-down creature face up can't be targeted.","oracle_id":"b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Brion Stoutarm leaves the battlefield after its ability has been activated but before it resolves, the game uses its last known information to determine that it had lifelink and you'll gain life for the damage it deals.","oracle_id":"b816b3cc-ae4b-4fb7-8b1a-e01ab83459a3","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the target player's library contains fewer cards than the sacrificed creature's power, all of those cards are put into that player's graveyard. That player won't lose the game until they try to draw from the empty library.","oracle_id":"d64e9152-ef24-4394-aeb0-9c3befc56549","published_at":"2019-06-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The number of cards the target player puts into their graveyard is equal to the power of the sacrificed creature as it last existed on the battlefield.","oracle_id":"d64e9152-ef24-4394-aeb0-9c3befc56549","published_at":"2019-06-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you don't have three cards in hand when instructed to discard three cards, you discard your hand.","oracle_id":"dc0593c2-ccb4-4648-a592-c5bcd121dc72","published_at":"2020-08-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Use the sacrificed creature's power as it last existed on the battlefield to determine how many cards you draw.","oracle_id":"dc0593c2-ccb4-4648-a592-c5bcd121dc72","published_at":"2020-08-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You draw and discard cards all while Greater Good's ability is resolving. Nothing can happen between the two, and no player may choose to take actions.","oracle_id":"dc0593c2-ccb4-4648-a592-c5bcd121dc72","published_at":"2020-08-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Use the power of the sacrificed creature as it last existed on the battlefield to determine the value of X.","oracle_id":"f61c1dc4-2f09-4b50-957f-ee656c659072","published_at":"2026-03-20","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The controller of Vedalken Orrery can cast nonland artifact, creature, enchantment, and sorcery cards any time they could cast an instant. This includes on other players' turns and during the upkeep step, draw step, combat phase, and end step.","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2004-12-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This applies only to casting spells. It does not, for example, change when you may activate abilities that can only be activated \"any time you could cast a sorcery\".","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
